{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuffixTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every suffix of every text ends at a leaf, the empty suffix included, and every internal node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a point where suffixes that agree so far go different ways, so the tree has at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes. A pattern is found in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") steps down from the root, and the leaves below where it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends are its occurrences."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let tree = SuffixTree(\"banana\")","tree.occurrences(of: \"ana\").map(\\.range)   \/\/ [3 ..< 6, 1 ..< 4]","tree.longestRepeatedSubstring?.range       \/\/ 3 ..< 6, \"ana\"","","let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring                \/\/ text 1, 3 ..< 7: \"abxa\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nodes are numbered in preorder from the root at 0, so a node’s subtree is the nodes from it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"just before the next node that is not its descendant. Children come in the order of the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that starts their edge: sorted when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", so the leaves are in the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their suffixes and match a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the same text; otherwise in the order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols first occur in the texts. Each text ends in a terminator of its own that sorts before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every symbol and belongs to no label."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its suffix links are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a directed graph, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Each node takes 32 bytes and each symbol 4 more, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"texts’ codes, which the tree keeps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The suffix tree of one or more texts: the compressed trie of all their suffixes, built left to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") (Ukkonen, “On-Line Construction of Suffix Trees”, 1995)."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:16SuffixStructures0A4TreeV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree.swift#L29","fileName":"SuffixTree.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}],"title":"SuffixTree","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuffixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/Occurrence","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/SuffixLinksView-swift.struct"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/init(texts:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/longestCommonSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/longestRepeatedSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/nodeCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/nodes","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/root","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/textCount"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":